    "diagnosis": "Schematic overview of adrenal cortical hormone biosynthesis and aberrant enzyme expression in various congenital adrenal hyperplasia (CAH) subtypes",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "By far the most common cause of CAH is 21-hydroxylase deficiency. Note that patients are unable to produce aldosterone and cortisol irrespectively of the subtype of CAH. Although patients with 21-hydroxylase and 11&beta;-hydroxylase&ndash;deficient CAH often display signs of virilization due to an excess of androgens, patients with 3&beta;-hydroxysteroid deficiency also display decreased levels of sex hormones.",
